						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=320.msg1772#msg1772"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=320.msg1772#msg1772">Re:And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #30 on:</b> September 24, 2003, 01:18:41 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							hmmm... this is fun, i just saw my guild up there ... not top 10, but never were aiming for it anyway... so it's just a nice thing to see...<br /><br />Here's what I'll add to the guilds in the lower tiers.<br /><br />- I know Brews have gotten into NToV... and have done the Burrower a few times now, as well as Grieg and IV<br />- AK can do HoT with ease, but hesitates on moving to WToV for faction... having fun with the named in Tier 1, and trying to key up and do tower mobs in BoT...<br />- AC allied with Ecce Necco, so if you put one up there, you'd probably want to put them both, or that alliance.<br /><br />All of the above guilds are casual though... raiding maybe two times a week...
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
