						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=320.msg1790#msg1790"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=320.msg1790#msg1790">Re:And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #33 on:</b> September 25, 2003, 01:18:38 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I agree with most of your list, RNwatcher, but that cheap shot at RoS was pretty stupid. &nbsp;Your accusation could have been valid if RoS never attempted RZTW before ascent helped them and got their strat from it, and if the majority of the guild was flagged because of it. &nbsp;Unfortunately, it just happens to be the opposite of the truth. &nbsp;RoS attempted RZTW a couple times before ascent invited them, and they got really close each time. &nbsp;It wasn't close to a majority of the raiding force that was flagged, so it isn't like Ascent held their hands at all. &nbsp;RoS went after RZTW not too long after and took him down solo, using the same strat that they used on their first attempts. &nbsp;I watched these attempts because my RL friend is in RoS, so I know what I'm talking about. &nbsp;Not sure what guild your in, that might be why you feel like bashing them, but maybe your just upset that ascent felt like inviting some of RoS to help them take out RZTW when they didn't have quite the numbers on to do it themselves.
						</td>
					</tr>
